==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Gold Nyanko Ranger''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
An anti-[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] crowd-controller with very high pierce through [[Wave Attack]]s. They can reach up to 533 range and have a 40% chance to [[Knockback]] target traits, making Gold Nyanko Ranger a genuinely decent anti-Angel crowd-controller for the early-game where many aren't readily available. But, unfortunately, she tends to become obsolete once [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]'s Target Angel [[Talents|Talent]] is unlocked. In truth, Knockback is a fairly middling ability, and given Gold Nyanko Ranger's long recharge, she cannot hope to hold the lines on her own against hordes of Angels unless very well-protected. Against Aku, she doesn't fare much better, since many of the more dangerous Aku have [[Shield]]s which negate her Knockback entirely. This makes her decent for frontline enemies like [[Aku Gory]] or [[Devil Wife]], but nearly useless against most other Aku.

[[Gold Silver Strike (Combo)|Gold Silver Strike]] does see powerful synergy with [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Nyanko Ranger]] against Aku, where it allows the [[:Category:Nyanko Rangers|Nyanko Rangers]] to survive nasty [[Death Surge]]s. It gives Red Nyanko Ranger viability against enemies which would have instantly evaporated it with Surge Attacks like [[Medu-san]] and the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]]. It is situationally useful on [[Ribbon Cat (Special Cat)|Pink Nyanko Ranger]] for similar reasons, and Gold Nyanko Ranger can even contribute a great deal with her crowd-controlling alongside the other Rangers.

Despite having great taste in color, Gold Nyanko Ranger is borderline unnecessary/outperformed by better units later in the game. She can find utility against enemies like [[St. Dober]] or Medu-san with her [[Cat Combo]], but struggles when pressured, especially with her painfully low HP. She meets a similar fate to [[Barista Cat (Special Cat)|Silver Nyanko Ranger]] in the [[Underground Labyrinth]] most of the time.

