==Trivia==
*Despite [[Ribbon Cat (Special Cat)|Ribbon Cat]]'s Japanese description claiming she is the only female [[:Category:Nyanko Rangers|Nyanko Ranger]] (紅一点 ''kōitten'' means the only female member of a group), Commander Cat's Japanese description contains the word 才色兼備 ''saishokukenbi'', meaning a woman who is both intelligent and beautiful.
*Unlike the first five Nyanko Rangers, Gold Nyanko Ranger and [[Barista Cat (Special Cat)|Silver Nyanko Ranger]] channel the souls of canids (fox and tanuki, respectively) rather than felids. This may be because they start as the enemies [[Possessed Gold Nyanko Ranger]] and [[Possessed Silver Nyanko Ranger]], and many other enemies are dogs.
*The Japanese names of Gold Nyanko Ranger and the [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]] unit [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]] both translate to "Gold Cat", but aren't the same. Gold Nyanko Ranger's is ゴールドにゃんこ ''Gōrudo Nyanko'', while Gold Cat's is 金ネコ ''Kin Neko''.

